<title>COMOROS: Doctors now say 52 survived hijack plane crash.</title>
<headline>Doctors now say 52 survived hijack plane crash.</headline>
<dateline>MORONI, Comoro Islands 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fifty-two people survived after a hijacked Ethiopian Airlines plane crashed into the sea off the Comoro Islands, medical sources said on Sunday, reducing the number from 54 earlier.</p>
<p>A source working for a security firm involved in the salvage operation said 50 bodies had been recovered from the wreckage. A medical team and scuba divers from the nearby French Reunion Island were now looking for more bodies and survivors at the scene, witnesses said.</p>
</text>
